x_value = subs(subs(subs(sol.x, 'c', subs(sol.c, 1)), 'a', subs(sol.a, 1)), 'b', subs(sol.b, 1));
This code substitutes the values of "a", "b", and "c" from the solution array into the expression for "x" and returns the resulting value. The use of "subs" function multiple times is necessary due to the nested structure of the equations.

